--TEST--
A written-out `string<K>` has every hole checked when the program compiles, with `as` and at a parameter: a hole naming no property is the unknown-member error at that hole or path part, a hole outside a set of values, an empty hole, an unclosed `{` and a lone `}` are `E0861` at the hole or the brace, and a `K` that is none of the three is `E0860` — `rule:types/string-holes`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Each hole of a string with holes is checked when the program compiles.
class Customer {
    public string $name = "Ada";
    private string $secret = "s";
}

class Order {
    public Customer $customer;
    public int $total = 40;

    public function constructor() {
        $this->customer = new Customer();
    }
}

class Query {
    public static function where(string<propertyPath<Order>> $condition): string {
        return $condition as string;
    }

    public static function columns(string<property<Customer>> $list): string {
        return $list as string;
    }

    public static function sort(string<'asc'|'desc'> $order): string {
        return $order as string;
    }

    public static function count(string<int> $text): void {}
}

// Two holes are misspelled, and each one is reported.
echo Query::where("{customer.nmae} = ? AND {totl} > 3"), "\n";
// `secret` is private.
echo Query::columns("{name}, {secret}"), "\n";
// `up` is not one of the values.
echo Query::sort("ORDER BY {up}"), "\n";
// An empty hole, a `}` with no `{` and a `{` with no `}`.
echo Query::where("{} = 1"), "\n";
echo Query::where("a } b"), "\n";
echo "{customer" as string<propertyPath<Order>> as string, "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0860]: `string<int>` names something its holes cannot be
   --> %s:30:41
   |
30 |     public static function count(string<int> $text): void {}
   |                                         ^^^ a key, a path or a set of strings is required here
   = help: a hole is a property name, a property path or one of a set of strings: write `string<property<T>>`, `string<propertyPath<T>>` or `string<'a'|'b'>`

error[E0405]: `Customer` has no public property `$nmae`
   --> %s:34:30
   |
34 | echo Query::where("{customer.nmae} = ? AND {totl} > 3"), "\n";
   |                              ^^^^ this part of the path is checked here
   = help: each part of a property path names a public property of the class the path has reached: `Customer` has `$name`

error[E0405]: `Order` has no public property `$totl`
   --> %s:34:45
   |
34 | echo Query::where("{customer.nmae} = ? AND {totl} > 3"), "\n";
   |                                             ^^^^ this part of the path is checked here
   = help: each part of a property path names a public property of the class the path has reached: `Order` has `$customer`, `$total`

error[E0405]: `Customer` has no public property `$secret`
   --> %s:36:31
   |
36 | echo Query::columns("{name}, {secret}"), "\n";
   |                               ^^^^^^ this hole is checked here
   = help: each hole names a public property of `Customer`, which has `$name`

error[E0861]: the hole `{up}` is not one of the allowed values
   --> %s:38:29
   |
38 | echo Query::sort("ORDER BY {up}"), "\n";
   |                             ^^ this hole is checked here
   = help: each hole is one of `asc`, `desc`

error[E0861]: a hole `{}` has no name in it
   --> %s:40:20
   |
40 | echo Query::where("{} = 1"), "\n";
   |                    ^ this brace
   = help: a hole is a name between `{` and `}`. Write `{{` for a `{` and `}}` for a `}` that are only text

error[E0861]: a `}` closes no hole
   --> %s:41:22
   |
41 | echo Query::where("a } b"), "\n";
   |                      ^ this brace
   = help: a hole is a name between `{` and `}`. Write `{{` for a `{` and `}}` for a `}` that are only text

error[E0861]: a `{` has no `}` after it
   --> %s:42:7
   |
42 | echo "{customer" as string<propertyPath<Order>> as string, "\n";
   |       ^ this brace
   = help: a hole is a name between `{` and `}`. Write `{{` for a `{` and `}}` for a `}` that are only text

